// Mixed argument types, refused -- and **the refusal moved** when `min` became a `native fn` on
// 2026-10-22. The arm said "expects every argument to be the same type, found int and float",
// which it worked out by comparing argument two against argument one. The resolver says which
// argument fixed `T` instead, because `min<T: Ord>(values: variadic T)` is where "the same type"
// was written down all along: one type parameter, so the second argument has nothing to disagree
// with except what the first already bound.
fn main() {
    print(min(3, 3.5))
}
